g table\n   - Check if \'ip\' command is available (run "which ip" or "ip addr")\n\n2. VERIFY the configuration:\n   - Check if interfaces have IP addresses assigned\n   - Check if default route exists (for endpoints)\n   - Check if interfaces are UP (not DOWN)\n\n3. FIX any issues you find:\n   - If \'ip\' command not found, install tools:\n     * For Alpine: "apk add --no-cache iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools"\n     * For Debian/Ubuntu/Kali: "apt-get update && apt-get install -y iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools"\n   - If interface has no IP, configure it based on expected commands\n   - If interface is DOWN, bring it UP: "ip link set <interface> up"\n   - If route missing, add it: "ip route replace default via <gateway>"\n\n4. VERIFY your fixes:\n   - Run "ip addr show" again to confirm IPs are configured\n   - Run "ip route show" to confirm routes exist\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Container name: clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-021549-56ae2e17-router\n- Use the node_config_tool with the exact container name\n- Always run verification commands after applying fixes\n- Be concise in your response\n\nBegin your diagnosis and configuration now.\n', 'role': 'user'}, {'content': "I'll start by diagnosing the current state of the router node. Let me first check the available interfaces and their IP addresses.", 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_69a91671d1054f1488d5bb22', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-021549-56ae2e17-router", "command": "ip addr show"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Output:\n1: lo: <LOOPBACK,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 65536 qdisc noqueue state UNKNOWN qlen 1000\n    link/loopback 00:00:00:00:00:00 brd 00:00:00:00:00:00\n    inet 127.0.0.1/8 scope host lo\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 ::1/128 scope host \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n2: eth0@if93: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP,M-DOWN> mtu 1500 qdisc noqueue state UP \n    link/ether 4e:d7:96:88:38:c5 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff\n    inet 172.20.20.14/24 brd 172.20.20.255 scope global eth0\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 3fff:172:20:20::e/64 scope global flags 02 \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::4cd7:96ff:fe88:38c5/64 scope link \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n95: eth1@if96: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP,M-DOWN> mtu 9500 qdisc noqueue state UP \n    link/ether aa:c1:ab:2a:e3:b2 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff\n    inet 10.0.0.1/24 scope global eth1\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::a8c1:abff:fe2a:e3b2/64 scope link \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n98: eth2@if97: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP,M-DOWN> mtu 9500 qdisc noqueue state UP \n    link/ether aa:c1:ab:82:86:00 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff\n    inet 10.0.1.1/24 scope global eth2\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::a8c1:abff:fe82:8600/64 scope link \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_69a91671d1054f1488d5bb22'}, {'content': 'Good! I can see that the router already has the correct IP addresses configured:\n- eth1: 10.0.0.1/24 ✓\n- eth2: 10.0.1.1/24 ✓\n\nNow let me check the routing table:', 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_ef680975180f4811876cd016', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-021549-56ae2e17-router", "command": "ip route show"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Output:\ndefault via 172.20.20.1 dev eth0 \n10.0.0.0/24 dev eth1 scope link  src 10.0.0.1 \n10.0.1.0/24 dev eth2 scope link  src 10.0.1.1 \n172.20.20.0/24 dev eth0 scope link  src 172.20.20.14 \n', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_ef680975180f4811876cd016'}, {'content': "Excellent! The routing table looks correct:\n- Default route via 172.20.20.1 dev eth0 ✓\n- 10.0.0.0/24 network via eth1 ✓\n- 10.0.1.0/24 network via eth2 ✓\n- 172.20.20.