dr show" to see all interfaces and their IPs\n   - Run "ip route show" to see routing table\n   - Check if \'ip\' command is available (run "which ip" or "ip addr")\n\n2. VERIFY the configuration:\n   - Check if interfaces have IP addresses assigned\n   - Check if default route exists (for endpoints)\n   - Check if interfaces are UP (not DOWN)\n\n3. FIX any issues you find:\n   - If \'ip\' command not found, install tools:\n     * For Alpine: "apk add --no-cache iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools"\n     * For Debian/Ubuntu/Kali: "apt-get update && apt-get install -y iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools"\n   - If interface has no IP, configure it based on expected commands\n   - If interface is DOWN, bring it UP: "ip link set <interface> up"\n   - If route missing, add it: "ip route replace default via <gateway>"\n\n4. VERIFY your fixes:\n   - Run "ip addr show" again to confirm IPs are configured\n   - Run "ip route show" to confirm routes exist\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Container name: clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-021549-56ae2e17-attacker\n- Use the node_config_tool with the exact container name\n- Always run verification commands after applying fixes\n- Be concise in your response\n\nBegin your diagnosis and configuration now.\n', 'role': 'user'}, {'content': "I'll start by diagnosing the current state of the container. Let me first check the interfaces and routing table.", 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_8e9240a9405e43759eb6250b', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-021549-56ae2e17-attacker", "command": "ip addr show"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Output:\n1: lo: <LOOPBACK,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 65536 qdisc noqueue state UNKNOWN group default qlen 1000\n    link/loopback 00:00:00:00:00:00 brd 00:00:00:00:00:00\n    inet 127.0.0.1/8 scope host lo\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 ::1/128 scope host proto kernel_lo \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n2: eth0@if92: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 1500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default \n    link/ether f6:f2:7a:ba:2c:ff brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 0\n    inet 172.20.20.13/24 brd 172.20.20.255 scope global eth0\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 3fff:172:20:20::d/64 scope global nodad \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::f4f2:7aff:feba:2cff/64 scope link proto kernel_ll \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n96: eth1@if95: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 9500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default \n    link/ether aa:c1:ab:3c:fa:51 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 1\n    inet 10.0.0.64/24 scope global eth1\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::a8c1:abff:fe3c:fa51/64 scope link proto kernel_ll \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_8e9240a9405e43759eb6250b'}, {'content': "Good! I can see that eth1 already has the correct IP address 10.0.0.64/24 configured and it's UP. Now let me check the routing table:", 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_9576e20f171f43c593b7e1e1', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-021549-56ae2e17-attacker", "command": "ip route show"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Output:\ndefault via 10.0.0.1 dev eth1 \n10.0.0.0/24 dev eth1 proto kernel scope link src 10.0.0.64 \n172.20.20.0/24 dev eth0 proto kernel scope link src 172.20.20.13 \n', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_9576e20f171f43c593b7e1e1'}, {'content': 'Excellent! The default route via 10.0.0.1 on eth1 is already configured. Let me also check if the necessary tools are available:', 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_f06528d161444b06ad2003d9', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-021549-56ae2e17-attacker", "command": "which ip"}